internal/monty vendors the Go wrapper for the Pydantic Monty Python
interpreter (https://github.com/fugue-labs/monty-go), taken at release
v0.2.0 (commit c5fede1ca39482ff3da7dc04c5fd569b8bc313b8, tag v0.2.0; the
vendored tree was checked out from the tag itself). Monty is distributed
under the MIT License; the LICENSE
file taken alongside the code is the upstream one and applies to this
directory rather than the repository-root licence.

The package code was copied and only mechanically changed: the package name
was rewritten from `montygo` to `monty` and error strings from
`montygo: …` to `monty: …`. Otherwise the files are upstream verbatim:

  * monty.go   — Runner, Limits, FunctionCall/FuncDef, Execute options
  * wasm.go    — the wazero instance plumbing and the pause/resume for
                 external function calls
  * errors.go  — MontyError

The upstream tests (monty_test.go) are not vendored; they use only the
standard library, but codetool_test.go in internal/coder covers the
behavior Strument depends on.

**The monty.wasm blob is NOT built from source here.** Rebuilding it needs
a Rust toolchain with the `wasm32-wasip1` target, and Strument deliberately
requires none (no cgo, no C toolchain — see CLAUDE.md). The pre-built blob
from the v0.2.0 release is vendored as-is:

  * monty.wasm — SHA-256
    d106ecf55330a09f5d54ea1dc159f8b6452db126a0bb161cd48d1585618a6ca8

Upgrading Monty — new wrapper code or a new blob — is a separate decision
with its own cost, and a reviewer should not have to guess that. The
wrapper is ~3 files by a single upstream author, which is why it is
vendored rather than taken as a module dependency.

The only dependencies are github.com/tetratelabs/wazero (pure Go) and
golang.org/x/sys.
